<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>ILLUSTRATIVE lm2d-xichang-2026-11-26 ascent (3DOF sim)</name><description>FLOWN 2026-11-26. T0 is the actual liftoff 2026-11-26T09:38:00Z (+180 s from the pre-flight NET 2026-11-26T09:35:00Z). Xinhua (26 Nov 2026 18:02:36): 17:38 Beijing liftoff on a Long March 2D from Xichang, Yaogan-49 Group 01 (遥感四十九号01组卫星) reached the planned orbit, Long March flight 681. http://www.news.cn/20261126/a0282f982c184654872225d3ccb64539/c.html LL2 id b00f0e9a-48d6-4f26-9cb5-7d19169ff7c4 is Launch Successful, net 2026-11-26T09:38:00Z, minute precision, last_updated 2026-11-26T11:20:00Z. UTC columns and KML &lt;when&gt; tags shifted +180 s. Elapsed times and ECEF geometry unchanged. Sim not re-run. ILLUSTRATIVE.
ILLUSTRATIVE ASCENT ECEF — Long March 2D / Unknown Payload (Xichang LC-3) — NOT OFFICIAL TELEMETRY
Method: first-principles 3DOF sim (/workspace/trajectory-deck/sim/ascent3dof.py): WGS-84 rotating Earth, J2, US76 drag,
TIMELINE mode: every ignition/cutoff/separation/fairing time is a published hard event; mdot=F_vac/(Isp_vac*g0); thrust SL/vac on ambient pressure.
FITTED (least squares vs published knots): vertical rise 17.00 s, kick 1.640 deg over 10 s, Cd 0.667, payload 1281 kg,
gravity turn, then linear-tangent steering tan(theta)=0.7050-0.002835*(t-t_ign stage 1).
Vehicle config: Long March 2D (configuration 2, two-stage) (sim/vehicles/lm2d.json; every number carries a source URL, derivation, or ASSUMPTION).
LM-2D TIMELINE mode: configuration-2 stage data (World Launch Vehicles 2nd ed. 2007 via huijiwiki) + SAST TYPICAL flight sequence (huijiwiki); all event times hard constraints. Typical sequence, not this flight&#x27;s.
ILLUSTRATIVE. PRE-FLIGHT. Unknown payload, Long March 2D, Xichang Launch Complex 3 (LC-3/LA-1). T0 is the LL2 NET 2026-11-26T09:35:00Z (Thu 26 Nov 1:35 a.m. PST; 17:35 BJT), status Go, window 09:30-09:52Z, net precision Hour. LL2 id b00f0e9a-48d6-4f26-9cb5-7d19169ff7c4, last_updated 2026-11-20T09:12:38Z, update &#x27;Added launch per NOTAMs; Payload and launch vehicle identities uncertain.&#x27;
Vehicle and stage data reused from the lm2d-taiyuan entry (vehicles/lm2d.json): configuration-2 masses and the SAST TYPICAL sequence via huijiwiki, S1 vacuum via the YF-20 ratio, verniers ASSUMED to run from S2 ignition to 705.1 s, 3.35 m fairing 860 kg ASSUMED, Cd transferred from the LM-3B fit. Event times are the typical sequence, not this flight&#x27;s. No altitude/range knots are published.
AZIMUTH 105.51 deg from NOTAM Q-line centres (ZPKM A6099/26 104.51 deg, ZGZU A6100/26 106.52 deg). TARGET ASSUMED: 500 km circular. The azimuth is southeast, non-rotating inclination 31.91 deg, so this is not the SSO shell used for the Taiyuan LM-2D. No deploy time is published. VEHICLE IDENTITY: LL2 names Long March 2D and flags the vehicle as uncertain. A Chinese Wikipedia future-launch row lists a Long March 2C to GTO from Xichang on 26 Nov with no clock; that row was not used.
Target (see launch config): insertion 500 km, apoapsis 500 km, fpa 0, launch azimuth 105.51 deg; payload 1281 kg.
Pad: 28.247059N 102.029008E. Frame: WGS-84 ECEF, positions km, velocities km/s (Earth-relative).
T0 used: 2026-11-26T09:38:00Z. Re-run with another T0 by shifting utc_iso only; ECEF geometry is Earth-fixed.
POST-CUTOFF: deploy time unpublished (No payload-deploy time is published (LL2 payload and orbit Unknown). The SAST typical sequence lists separation at 737.1 s, but that time is not this flight&#x27;s, so it is not used.). From insertion T+705.1 s the stage is propagated for TWO revolutions (osculating period 94.62 min) on the inferred insertion orbit (same WGS-84/J2/US76-drag model); rows tagged -coast/-burn.
POST-CUTOFF end T+12059 s: inferred insertion orbit, +2 revs (deploy time unpublished): alt 499.84 km, osculating 498.7 x 501.8 km, i 33.893 deg.
POST-CUTOFF note: Typical-sequence residual-propellant venting after separation is not modelled.</description>
